[39;49m[K[2m• [22mA terminal emulator is an application that gives you a text-based window for interacting with a computer. It lets you[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  type commands and see the responses from programs, shells, or remote systems. Instead of clicking buttons and menus,[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  you work by entering instructions as text. The emulator handles details like displaying characters, colors, cursor[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  movement, and scrollback history. It can also connect to other machines through tools such as SSH, making it useful[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  for managing servers. In short, it recreates the behavior of an old physical terminal inside a modern graphical[39m[49m[0m
